== Overview ==
With the addition of the cooking system, players can cook up various combinations of items to boost their stats temporarily. When a cooking item is eaten, HP and SP are recovered by a certain amount and stats increase by a certain amount. The higher the grade of cooking item consumed, the greater the stat boost. When consumed, stats will increase for 20 minutes, and stack with existing support skills (such as [[Blessing]], [[Increase AGI]], etc). 

If several food items of the same type (Stat) are consumed, the highest level one takes precedence. Therefore, if a lower level food item is consumed while a higher level one is active, the low level one is ignored. 

To make items with the cooking skill, a training quest must be done.  After being trained, this allows you to use a cooking kit. The better the kit is, the higher the success rate to create an item. A cookbook (the recipes) of the correct level is also needed. Recipes exist for level 1-10 cooking items. The required items as listed in the recipe must also be obtained. 

Bonus from cooked food (and item mall food depending on server) is lost if a character dies while still under the effects of the food item.

When the cooking kit is double clicked, it will bring up a list of possible dishes that can be created with the items and recipes (cookbooks) in a player's inventory. However just like the blacksmith hammer during weapon creation, the cooking kit is consumed during cooking. Success rate is affected by [[DEX]] and [[LUK]], also higher level of recipe difficulty decreases success rate, the cooking set used will also affect success rate, and finally the more food you cook will give a small boost in success rate.

