[[Category: General Information]]
[[Category:Cash Shop]]

=Overview=
You can enchant your costume on a building in [[Malangdo]] {{navi|malangdo|115|150}}. There are 3 [[NPC]] responsible for enchanting inside: '''Designer Heidam''', '''Aver De Dosh''' and '''Lace La Zard'''.<br>
[[File:Malangdo-Costume.png]]

===Overall Process===
The general process has 3 layers of RNG:
#Get an enchantable costume.
#Buy desired costume loot box, open it, and hope to get desired costume.
#Exchange costume and hope to get desired enchant stone.
#Use enchant stone and hope enchant succeeds.

=Enchanting a Costume=
Talk to '''Aver De Dosh''' {{navi|mal_in01|22|113}} to enchant Headgear costume and '''Lace La Zard''' {{navi|mal_in01|20|107}} for Garment costume.
*You must have the costume equipped and the stone in the inventory to perform the enchantment.
**To enchant a Headgear middle costume, take off the Headgear upper costume first.
**To enchant a Headgear lower costume, take off the Headgear upper and middle costumes first.
*Even without a stone, NPC will still tell you if equipped costume is enchantable or not.
*A single costume headgear (upper, middle, or lower) can have both a [[Costume Enchantment Stones|stats effect enchant]] and a [[Costume Enchantment Stones#Visual Effect Stones|visual effect enchant]] simultaneously. Costume garments can have a Garment Stone and a Dual Stone simultaneously.
*Stats effect enchantment has a 50% success chance, while visual effect enchantment has a 100% success chance.
**Enchant on a costume can be changed by re-enchanting the costume with a new stone. 
**If enchant '''fails''', then the stone selected for the attempt and any previous enchant in that slot will disappear. However, the costume and any enchants or effects in other slots are safe.
**Dual stone go to costume garment's dual slot only.
**[Named] Costumes will lose the name whether enchant succeeds or fails.

*A costume that takes multiple slot can be enchanted multiple times based on the number of slots the costume takes.
**Upper headgear enchant will take slot 1, middle headgear enchant will take slot 2, lower headgear enchant will take slot 3, and visual effect enchant (any position) will take slot 4.
*[[Costume Enchantment Stones#Visual Effect Stones|Visual effect enchant]] can be removed at 100% success rate by first choosing ''Apply effect'', then paying 99,800 zeny. No stone given back.

= Enchantable Costume =
''See '''[[Enchantable Costume]]''' for detailed information.''

= Way to get Enchantment Stones =
==Exchanging from Costumes==
'''Designer Heidam''' {{navi|mal_in01|20|124}} will trade 1 Costume into 1 Enchant Stone. He will take a costume '''RANDOMLY FROM YOUR INVENTORY'''. So, it is a good idea to put some costume you want to keep on cart first.

