==Introduction==
The crystal synthesis quests provide players with enhanced gears, synthesized with energy crystals. They also provide three hours buffs which also reward crystals.

Talk to '''Reno''' {{navi|moc_paraup|41|167}} in [[Eden Group|Eden Group Headquarters]] 2F to start with the quests.

:[[File:EdenGroupCrystalSynthesis Reno.jpg|250px]]

Reno also can compress energy crystal:<br>
{{Item List|id=6623|item=Rough Energy Crystal|num=10|simple=yes}} = {{Item List|id=6624|item=Purified Energy Crystal|num=1|simple=yes}}<br>
{{Item List|id=6624|item=Purified Energy Crystal|num=5|simple=yes}} = {{Item List|id=6625|item=High Energy Crystal|num=1|simple=yes}}

Rough and Purified Crystals can be sold and traded between accounts, but High Energy Crystals are account-bound.

==Energy Crystal Buffs==
{{repeatable|cooldown=23 hour}}
You may request an energy crystal buff from Reno. These buffs last for three hours (with a buff icon), providing a boost to atk and matk, and after that period of time, you may talk to Reno to be rewarded with 2~4 energy crystals at random. The 23 hour cooldown starts when you get the crystals, not when you start the quest, so these can't be done every day. You can only receive one buff at a time, however, each of the three has its own cooldown time, which makes it possible, for example, to take a 80+ level buff, while you have a cooldown on a 90+ level one.

