== Overheating ==
If your Madogear receives too much damage, it will overheat and you will be inflicted with the [[overheat]] status. You can increase the damage threshold of your Madogear by learning [[Remodel Mainframe]], and prevent infliction of the status by using [[Cooldown]].

[[File:Overheat_Counter.png]]

Note: Overheat is not fatal, but will lower the player's HP to 1 continuously until the Madogear is removed or [[Cooldown]] is used.

== Limitations ==
'''''Receiving skills:'''''

When wearing Madogear, the player is unable to '''receive''' certain supportive skills, such as:
*[[Increase Agility]]
*[[Heal]]
*[[Adrenaline Rush]]
*[[Coluseo Heal]]**

However, the player can receive Increase Agility from [[Cantocandidus]].

'''**Note''':When Coluseo skill is cast within a party, the Heal will stop being delivered depending on the Party member list, from top to bottom. For example: If the Mado Mechanic is party member #3, no heal will be delivered to party members 3-12. This seems to be a bug that also can be seen when a party member receives Undead Status. It is recommended to put any Madogear Mechanics to the bottom of the party.

'''''Using skills:'''''

When wearing Madogear, the player is unable to '''actively cast''' non-Mechanic skills. However, there are exceptions. 

The following non-mechanic skills can be cast by a Madogear user:
*[[Greed]]
*[[Teleport]]
* Skills that are cast by using an item/scroll (unless it's a skill you can't receive - see above) such as:
**[[Blessing]] 
**[[Assumptio]]

*Any Auto-cast Skills from equipment that triggers when being attacked or attacking, such as:
**[[Greed]]
**[[Assumptio]]
**[[Heal]]
**[[Increase Agility]] 
**[[Adrenaline Rush]] 


'''Note''': Skills enabled by equipments, such as [[Heal]] from Vitata Card, can't be used. 
Skills that don't work on Madogear users in general, such as Heal, Increase Agility and Adrenaline Rush, '''only work when''' being '''auto-cast''' with Equipments. 



