Consequently, the Party Leader must ensure all Party Members are within the Rank's level range.
* Any members outside this range will be denied entry to the instance by '''Leticia'''.

=== Tower Difficulty ===

Increasing the Tower's Difficulty before beginning the instance will not only make it more challenging but also offer up greater EXP rewards per monster and as a reward every 5 Tower Levels.

The default Difficulty Level is set to 1. To change the difficulty, '''Leticia''' requires {{Item List 2|id=1000372|item=Meteorite Dust|num=10|simple=yes}}, then the party leader can select a difficulty from 1 through 5. You only required to adjust difficuly and pay Meteorite Dust once at the start. You will not be able to change the difficulty again until the instance duration is over.

Increasing the Tower Difficulty will also increase the following:
* Number of monsters per floor.
* Monster's overall damage is increased. 
** Observed: monsters hit 2x harder on Difficulty 5 compared to Difficulty 1.
* Monster's health is increased. 
** Observed: monsters HP on Difficulty 5 is 2x compared to Difficulty 1.
* Monster's defense is increased. 
** Observed: Difficulty 1 has 10% damage reduction while Difficulty 5 has 50% damage reduction.
* Experience granted from monsters is increased. See [[Sunken Tower#Rewards|Rewards]] section for details.
* Bonus Experience granted from every 5th Floor Rewards are increased. See [[Sunken Tower#Rewards|Rewards]] section for details.

After the Party Leader selects the difficulty and initiates instance, monsters will spawn immediately. Players must clear all monsters on the floor before they can proceed to the next floor.

=== Tower Progress ===

The instance has an endless amount of floors, even beyond floor 100, and progress is only limited by the 30 minute timer.

When all monsters are defeated, the '''Dimensional Device''' at the end of the floor will allow the Party Leader to send all members to the next floor. However, every 5 floors, the '''Dimensional Device''' will grant bonus Experience and a chance to acquire {{Item List 2|id=1000372|item=Meteorite Dust|num=1|simple=yes}}. See [[Sunken Tower#Rewards|Rewards]] section for details.
* All party members must talk to the '''Dimensional Device''' to be rewarded. Only the Party Leader can forcibly proceed the party to the next floor and doing so will ignore the unrewarded members requirement to click the Device at the cost of gaining no bonus Experience. This option is in place to avoid time loss for players utilizing multiple characters/clients at the same time.

Leticia will announce the final 10 minutes of the instance in 1 minute increments. When the time ends, all party members will be kicked back to [[Alberta]].
* There are no NPCs or Portals to exit this instance. You must use a Butterfly Wing-type item or die to respawn to town.
* When a party member dies, '''Leticia''' won't allow you to keep advancing floors until you revive them.
*You are unable to progress floors unless all the party members are online and in the same map.

== Monsters ==

* Monsters will not drop any items in this instance.
* Monsters do not use any skills, only normal [[Neutral]] property attacks.
* There are no Boss Monsters in this instance.
* Monsters per floor are completely random in race / size / elemental property. 
* Monsters will also change their natural element upon spawn through a NPC skill. 
** For example, {{Skill List|id=162|skill=NPC_CHANGEWATER|simple=yes}} will change the element to [[Water]].
* All monsters have {{Skill List|id=771|skill=NPC_RELIEVE_ON|simple=yes}} which reduces damage they take by a percentage. This percentage increases based on the Tower Difficulty level.
* A Monster's name will be based on the current floor, such as “''Basement Floor 11 Variant'' ”.
* Upon entering and initiating the [[Sunken Tower]] instance, '''Leticia''' will give a hint about which element the majority of monsters will become when they spawn. The element she mentions means that there will be more enemies with that element present throughout the entire dungeon.

